## Requirements

- Python 3.11+
- A Telegram account (two recommended) with API credentials from
  [my.telegram.org](https://my.telegram.org)
- A Telegram bot token from [@BotFather](https://t.me/BotFather) for the
  admin panel
- Railway account (for cloud deployment) or any Linux VPS

Install dependencies:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

## Environment Variables

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in all values.

### Required

| Variable | Description |
|---|---|
| `API_ID` | Telegram API ID from my.telegram.org |
| `API_HASH` | Telegram API hash from my.telegram.org |
| `PHONE_NUMBER` | Phone number for Account 1 (e.g. `+821012345678`) |
| `BOT_TOKEN` | Admin bot token from @BotFather |
| `ADMIN_USER_ID` | Your Telegram user ID (integer) |

### Account 1 session (choose one)

| Variable | Description |
|---|---|
| `SESSION_STRING` | Base64 string session — **recommended for Railway** |
| `SESSION_NAME` | Local session file path (default: `sessions/userbot`) |

### Account 2 (optional)

| Variable | Description |
|---|---|
| `PHONE_NUMBER_2` | Phone number for Account 2 |
| `SESSION_STRING_2` | String session for Account 2 |
| `SESSION_NAME_2` | Local session file path for Account 2 |

### Optional

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `TARGET_GROUP` | — | Target group ID (can also be set via admin bot) |
| `DATABASE_PATH` | `data/job_bot.db` | Path to SQLite database file |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | `INFO` | Logging level (`DEBUG`, `INFO`, `WARNING`) |
| `DEDUP_WINDOW_HOURS` | `24` | Hours to remember forwarded posts for dedup |
| `DEDUP_SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD` | `0.85` | Fuzzy match threshold (0.0–1.0) |

> **Railway auto-detection:** If `RAILWAY_ENVIRONMENT` is set (Railway injects
> this automatically), `DATABASE_PATH` defaults to `/data/job_bot.db` so that
> attaching a Volume at `/data` is sufficient — no extra variable needed.

